+# Agent Note: macOS kernel process observations
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-15-macos-kernel-process-observations.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Terminal readiness needs fresh descendant observations. Spawning `ps` for every observation blocks the host while the utility gathers information beyond the parentage and start identity required by the inspector.
+
+## Decision
+
+The macOS inspector uses the existing Koffi dependency to call `sysctl` with `KERN_PROC_ALL` or `KERN_PROC_PID`, the kernel source used by [Apple's ps](https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/adv_cmds/blob/main/ps/ps.c). Each call owns its buffer; no table or identity cache crosses calls. The [point-query decision](2026-09-15-macos-identity-point-query.md) continues to require a new selected-PID observation immediately before signalling.
+
+The reader decodes the LP64 `kinfo_proc` fields shared by arm64 and x64. A C SDK oracle asserts sizes, offsets, and selectors for both architectures. The buffer has twice the estimated capacity to accommodate process creation between sizing and reading. Further growth, syscall failures, and malformed results throw; an incomplete table never proves quiescence.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Cache or reduce discovery polls.** Rejected because a descendant may reparent before a later observation can retain its identity.
+
+**Read every PID through libproc BSD info.** Rejected because that query restricts cross-user access; treating inaccessible rows as absent weakens discovery.
+
+**Add a native helper artifact.** Rejected because Koffi already ships in this provider and a helper adds build, packaging, and launch responsibilities for this synchronous query.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Process inspection creates no child process and adds no dependency, asynchronous work, or lifecycle owner. Whole-table reads remain fresh. Identities encode epoch seconds rather than locale-formatted dates, remain private, and retain second precision; session omission, presence-only liveness, and observational containment remain unchanged.
+
+Focused tests reject invalid/truncated results and failed queries, compare real rows with `ps` across user identities, and exercise identity-fenced signals. The SDK oracle validates x64 layout but is not an x64 runtime test. Native runtime evidence is macOS arm64; other OS paths retain their implementations.
